  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1255 PM MDT Sat Apr 18 2026\n\nRidge of high pressure will continue to build into East Idaho \nfor the next several days. Despite warming temperature trend, \nanother night of sub-freezing temperatures is on tap tonight, \nwith a FREEZE WARNING remaining in place. Temperatures cold \nenough to support a Hard Freeze look to be relegated to areas \nalong/north of US-26 tonight. Sunday night the cold temperatures\nretreat further. A FROST ADVISORY may be needed for a few \nzones, but temperatures do look to be above freezing. Will hold \noff on additional headlines for now. Daytime highs continue to \nclimb as well, reaching into the 70s for most lower elevation \nareas both Monday and Tuesday. \n\nWe are still looking at the next system arriving by mid week as\na broad Pacific low shifts inland. Precipitation looks to\nincrease across the region by Tuesday night, with the best\nchances for rainfall and a few thunderstorms on Wednesday. Gusty\nwinds look likely as the system impacts the region late in the\nweek, especially Tuesday and Wednesday. Cooler temperatures\narrive as well, but not as cold as the past few days. Snow\nlevels still look to be around 6500 ft, so snow will be\nrelegated to higher elevations. Ensemble clusters have come into\nbetter agreement through Wednesday, but diverge for the\nremainder of the forecast as the trough progresses through the\nregion.",
